# ============================================================================
# Colorado Mesh Newsletter — .gitignore
# Keep community Discord data, tokens, and machine state OUT of git.
# The CODE and PROCESS are public; the raw private chatter is not.
# See DATA-PRIVACY.md for the why.
# NOTE: git does NOT support trailing inline comments on pattern lines —
#       every pattern is on its own line, comments on their own lines.
# ============================================================================

# --- Discord raw data & triage intermediates (PRIVATE — never commit) ---
**/data/
**/raw-*.jsonl
**/*shortlist*.jsonl
**/candidates*.json
**/stage1*.md

# --- gatherer state (per-channel high-water marks) ---
.state/
**/state.json

# --- secrets / tokens / credentials ---
*.env
.env
*token*
*secret*
*.pem
*.key

# --- per-issue working scratch that isn't for publication ---
**/items-list.md
**/PICK-LIST.md
# Photos: keep the raw source dump + contact sheet PRIVATE, but DO commit the
# web-sized images an issue actually publishes (they ship in the PDF anyway and
# the markdown draft needs them to preview). Selected images are named *_web.*.
**/photos/contact-sheet.html
**/photos/*.jpg
**/photos/*.png
!**/photos/*_web.jpg
!**/photos/*_web.png

# --- python / os cruft ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.venv/
venv/

# ============================================================================
# WHAT *IS* COMMITTED (these are intentionally NOT ignored):
#   tools/        - all the scripts (transparent)
#   templates/    - the markdown + PDF templates
#   brand/        - official brand assets (from Colorado-Mesh/branding)
#   docs/         - DESIGN, EDITORIAL, voice guide
#   LIFECYCLE.md, README.md, DATA-PRIVACY.md
#   issues/<month>/draft.md          - the APPROVED, reviewed markdown
#   issues/<month>/newsletter-*.pdf  - the final published PDF
# ============================================================================
